[h1]Worker Optimizer[/h1]
[b]Auto-assign workers to suitable jobs with one click.[/b]

Match your residents' specialties to your settlement's workplaces. Worker Optimizer evaluates your current workforce, staffs minimum crews first and then fills extra positions with suitable workers.

[h2]Features[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]One-click assignment:[/b] evaluate and assign your current workforce from an always-visible icon.
[*][b]Better job matches:[/b] considers guild specialties, productivity and job requirements.
[*][b]Minimum crews first:[/b] fill feasible minimum crews before adding suitable workers to extra positions.
[*][b]Construction reserve:[/b] keep residents available for building, using your saved reserve or 1 resident by default.
[*][b]Preserve protected workers:[/b] leave paused buildings and unsupported warehouse workplaces unchanged.
[/list]

[h2]Getting started[/h2]
Subscribe and restart after Steam downloads the update. Use either Workshop or a local installation, never both.

Click the lower-left assignment icon. It shows when assignment is running and becomes available again when the run ends. Check the assigned workers in the game's building and resident windows.

[b]Recommended timing:[/b] Run assignment at night or just after a new day starts. Running it during the day may cause assignment errors.

[h2]Preview information[/h2]
[b]v0.3.1-preview[/b] targets Whiskerwood 0.7.209.0 on Windows. [b]In-game validation is pending.[/b] Try a separate save first. Assignment covers supported active workplaces; available workers, the construction reserve and job requirements determine which buildings can be staffed.

This update skips unsupported warehouse workplaces while keeping their existing workers. It addresses a rejected assignment that could stop a run at those buildings.

